erences, and I'd put q above that threshold. That points toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out the threshold for this twin prisoner's dilemma, where both copies share the same model and essay. With the payoffs converted to utilities, the cooperation threshold comes to 5/7, about 0.714.\n\nI'm checking whether the correlation between the two copies is high enough to clear the 0.714 threshold. They share the same model, essay, and decision theory, so their reasoning is symmetric despite the surface differences, and I'd put q above that threshold. That points toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9453,"completion_tokens":693,"total_tokens":10146,"cost":0.051672,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.051672,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037812,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01386},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":268,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}